  "worked_solution": "Since we are given that the volume of water in the pail is $30$ cubic centimeters, the time can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30 & =7\\sqrt{s}+2 \\\\ 7\\sqrt{s} & =28 \\\\ \\sqrt{s} & =4 \\\\ s & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe instantaneous rate at which the volume of water in the pail is changing when $s=16$ seconds is equal to ${V}^{\u2032}(16).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(s)$ with respect to $s$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(7\\sqrt{s}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(7{s}^{1/2}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{s}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=16$ gives\n\n$$\n{V}^{\u2032}(16)=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{16}}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of water in the pail is changing when $s=16$ seconds is $\\frac{7}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
